hadiths[48]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2961","Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) said that Sayyidna Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him) used to make grandfather a third partner with his brothers."
"2962","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) used to share a third of the grandfather with his brothers, and did not reduce it."
"2963","On the authority of Ismail, Amir (al-Shaabi) said: In the matter of grandfather, follow what the people (the scholars) have agreed upon. Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: That is, adopt the saying of Sayyiduna Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"2964","Qatadah, may Allah have mercy on him, said: Sayyidna Zaid bin Thabit (RA) divided the inheritance of the sister, mother, husband and grandfather by 27 and gave six shares to the mother, nine to the husband, eight to the grandfather and four to the sister."
"2965","Sayyiduna Ibn Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: The first grandmother in Islam who was given a share of the inheritance is the father's mother and her son was Hayat."
"2966","On the authority of Taaws, may God have mercy on him, Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, narrated that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave a sixth (sixth) to Jeddah."
"2967","It was narrated from Saeed bin Al-Musayyib, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Umar (may God be pleased with him) made the grandmother an heir along with her son."
"2968","Ibrahim Ibn Maisrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave six-sixths to three grandmothers (grandmothers). Mansoor bin Mu'tamar said: I said to Ibrahim: What are those sects? So they said: Two, your paternal grandmother (grandmother) and your maternal grandmother."
"2969","Ibrahim bin Maisrah said: I was informed by Hasan (Basri) that Jeddah (grandmother) will inherit in the presence of her son."
"2970","Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said: The father's mother's mother will not be an heir. If her son who is close (to the deceased) does not become an heir, how will she herself be an heir?"
"2971","Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain Radiyallahu Anhu said: Jeddah (grandmother) will inherit if her son is alive."
"2972","Imam Zuhri Ibn Shahab, may God have mercy on him, said: A woman (grandmother or grandmother) came to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr and said that my grandson or great-grandson has died and I have heard that I have a share in the inheritance, so what is for me? Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddique (RA) said: I did not hear about this from the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), but I will ask the people, so when they had offered the Zuhr prayer, he said: Did any of you hear anything about Jeddah (grandmother or grandmother) from the Messenger of Allah (PBUH)? Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) said: Yes, I have heard. Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) said: Have you heard? He said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him one-sixth. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddique (RA) said: Does anyone else know about it besides you? Sayyidna Muhammad bin Muslimah (RA) testified that Sayyidna Mughirah (RA) spoke the truth, so Sayyidna Abu Bakr Siddique (RA) gave Sadus to this woman. Then a woman came to Sayyiduna Umar with a similar problem and she said: I do not remember that I heard anything about this from the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, but I will ask the people. One-sixth (one-sixth) will be divided between the two."
"2973","It was narrated from Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Ali and Sayyidna Zayd, may God be pleased with them, said: When the jiadats are the same, then three jiadats will be inherited."
"2974","(Ibn Shihab) On the authority of Zuhri, may Allah have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) did not give a share of the inheritance to the grandmother in the presence of her son."
"2975","Sayyiduna Ibn Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: There is no inheritance for the Jadaat, it is a donation for them, whether the Jadaat are close or distant relatives."
"2976","Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (RA) said: Jeddah will be the heir in the presence of the son."
"2977","Shaabi said: Four jiadats came to Masrooq, may God have mercy on him, in a row, out of them, he expelled the grandfather's mother (i.e. the great-grandmother) and declared the other three heirs, two paternal grandmothers, namely the mother's mother (nani) and the father's mother (dadi) and his mother's grandmother (parnani)."
"2978","It was narrated from Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said about the daughter and the granddaughter: Half (for the daughter) and one sixth (for the granddaughter), the remaining child will be returned to the daughter."
"2979","It is narrated from al-Qamah that when the issue of paternal brothers and mother was brought to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, he gave a third to the paternal brothers and gave the rest of the property to the mother and said: Whoever (the heir of the deceased) does not have an Asaba, the mother will be counted among his Asaba."
"2980","Hasan (bin Salih bin Muslim) narrated from his father that he asked Imam Amir al-Shaabi, may God have mercy on him: A man died and left his daughter, and there is no known heir besides her. He said: All the wealth will belong to the daughter."
"2981","It was narrated from Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (RA) did not return the remaining inheritance to the paternal brother along with the mother, and did not return the remaining property to Jeddah when the owner of the duty was present with him, and did not return the remainder to the granddaughter when the real daughter was present, and did not return it to the wife and husband, and Sayyidna Ali (RA) used to return the remaining property to each sharer except the wife and husband."
"2982","Al-Khajri bin Zayd said that the case of a daughter and sister was brought to Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (RA), so he gave half to the daughter, and deposited the other half in the treasury, and this effect was narrated by Yazid bin Haroon on the authority of Muhammad bin Salim, on the authority of Sha’bi, and on the authority of Al-Khajri (bin Zayd)."
"2983","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said about the son of Laan that his inheritance will be for his mother. \n That is, the father will not be his heir like the son of Al-Zina."
"2984","Ibrahim bin Tahman said: I heard a man ask Ata bin Abi Rabah about the descendants of those who curse, to whom will their inheritance be? He said: It will be for his mother and her mother's children."
"2985","Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said: Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with him, said about Ibn Al-Malaana (i.e., the boy born after Laan): He who leaves his maternal brother and mother: the maternal brother has one-sixth and the mother one-third, then the rest will be divided between them, so the brother will have one-third and the mother will have two-thirds."
"2986","It was narrated from Imam al-Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, about Ibn al-Mala'ina: The one who left the nephew and the grandfather (or grandfather), said that all the wealth will belong to the nephew. (Because after Laan, it is not correct to relate to the grandfather, so he will not inherit. And Allah knows best)"
"2987","Sayyiduna Zayd bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated about the inheritance of Ibn Al-Ma'ina that one-third is for the mother and the remaining two-thirds is for Bait-ul-Mal."
"2988","It was narrated from Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said (about the inheritance of Ibn Al-Mala'ina): His inheritance is for his mother, and those who are related to his mother will pay the dowry from him (if there is a delay). \n And Qatadah, may God have mercy on him, said: Hasan, may God have mercy on him, narrated: One-third is for the mother, and the rest of the wealth belongs to her mother's family."
"2989","Qatadah (may God have mercy on him) reported that Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Ibn Mas’ud (may God be pleased with him) said about the son of Al-Malaana: He who leaves Jeddah and his Akhiafi (maternal brother), one-third to Jeddah (Umm al-Alam) and the remaining children to the maternal brothers are two-thirds."
"2990","Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: His mother, the mother of Ibn Al-Mala'ina, will inherit."
"2991","The previous example is mentioned in this document as well."
"2992","Abdullah bin Ubayd bin Umayr said: I wrote to my brother in Bani Zureeq that what the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, had decided about Ibn Al-Ma'ana. He replied that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decided it in favor of the mother, because the mother is the place of the mother and father for the boy after Laan. \n And Sufyan said: All the wealth will be for the mother because \mother\"" will be in the rank of both mother and father."""
"2993","On the authority of Hasan, may God have mercy on him, about Ibn Al-Ma'ina: He who left behind his mother and his mother's family, he said: A third belongs to the mother, and the child belongs to the mother's family."
"2994","Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with them) said: Ibn al-Ma'ina's family is his mother's family (i.e., in the absence of an heir, all the wealth will belong to him)."
"2995","Yunus said: Hasan, may God have mercy on him, used to say: The inheritance of the son of the cursed belongs to his mother. Yunus said: I said, if his maternal brother is also present? Said: If he has a maternal brother, then there will be Sadas for him."
"2996","Imam al-Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: The son of the accursed: his mother will inherit him and take her share of his wealth, and all this wealth will go to Bait al-Mal."
"2997","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If the husband and wife curse, they will be separated, then they will never be husband and wife, and the boy will be attributed to the mother, it will be said that so-and-so is the son of such and such a woman, she (the cursed woman) will be an usba for that boy, that boy will be his heir and she will be the boy's heir. And whoever taunts this boy, son of Al-Zina, will be flogged. (Eighty lashes are for slander)."
"2998","Shaibani (Sulaiman bin Abi Sulaiman) narrated to Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, about the son of Al-Mutala'inin that his mother's Asaba would inherit him and pay the dowry on his behalf."
"2999","On the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated about the son of al-Mutala’ina: The one whose father is not (known), his mother and his maternal brothers and his mother’s relatives will be his heirs."
"3000","It is narrated from Numan that Makhool, may God have mercy on him, was asked about the inheritance of the son of the cursed, who will it be for? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made his inheritance special for his mother because she was caught in this (curse) trouble because of her, and he made his (heritage) special for his maternal brothers. \n Makhool, may God have mercy on him, said: If a mother dies and leaves her son, then her son also dies for whom there was an inheritance, then his inheritance will go to the maternal brothers, because this inheritance belongs to their (maternal brothers) mother and maternal grandfather, and the maternal grandfather will have one-sixth of the inheritance of his granddaughter, and the maternal grandfather will inherit only in that case because he is the father of the mother, and the maternal brother will inherit from his mother and the maternal grandfather will inherit from his daughter, because he The inheritance of the (illegitimate son) belongs to the mother, so the property that belongs to this boy belongs to the heirs of the mother. If there is no other heir, then the inheritance will be in the possession of the grandfather."
"3001","On the authority of Ikrimah, Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, narrated that some people came to Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with them, with a dispute about the son of the accursed, then the people (asba) of his father's side also came to demand their inheritance. And they decided his inheritance in favor of his (Wald al-Mala'ina's) mother and declared the mother as his Asaba."
"3002","Muhammad bin Ali narrated from Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) about a person who is neither a man nor a woman (i.e. eunuch), in what status he will be given an inheritance (male or female)."
"3003","On the authority of Sha'bi, may Allah have mercy on him, Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said about the eunuch (eunuch): In terms of the place of urination, he will inherit."
"3004","Abu Hani said: Amir (al-Shaabi) may Allah have mercy on him was asked about a child who is neither male nor female, neither the whole body is male nor the whole body is female, urine and faeces come out of his trunk, what will be his share in the inheritance? He replied: Half of it will be as a man and half as a woman."
"3005","It was narrated on the authority of Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) was asked about Kalalah, and he said: I express my opinion about it. I want to reject what Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) said."
"3006","Uqbah bin Amir Jahni said: Nothing tired the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, as much as Kalala tired them."
"3007","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Kalalah is that (the deceased) should not leave a father and a son (who will be his heir)."
"3008","It is narrated from Saeed (Saad in some hadiths) that he recited this verse: «And if a man inherits the inheritance. . . . . .» [An-Nisaa: 12/4] That is: Those whose inheritance is taken away, whether male or female (i.e. not having a father or son), and if he has a brother or a sister, then each of them has a sixth share."
